    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιφῶν</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶντος</span>,
			ὁ, properly part. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμφιφάω,</span> cake offered to Munychian
		Artemis <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by double light,</i>
			i.e. either <i>surrounded by lighted tapers,</i> or <i>offered
				when sun and moon were both visible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				156
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				67
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				94.55
			</span></i>.</div>
